            "review_id": "REV_16913773_p1_3",
            "reviewer_id": "User_16913773_1_3",
            "review_title": "Review at Pho Tau Bay",
            "review_text": "kvinh2013\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam175 contributions\n1\n3 Locations 1 Family Feud\nMar 2019 • Family\nPhở Tàu Bay history goes back to 1954 when the patriarch of this phơ dynasty, fleeing from the north (birth place of phở), settled here in Ho Chi Minh. As his pure northern style of phở grew in popularity so did his family's fortune. As he retired, he left the restaurant and his closely guarded recipe to his two daughters. Soon after, the two daughters feuded and split the restaurant in two, operating one next to the other, separated only by a wall. That's two locations. Sometime later a defecting employee stole the recipe and went to Orange county, California to open a third location. Fortunately for us all, all three locations produce good phở. I am bias toward the right location on Ly Thai Tổ after trying out all three. Once in there, don't try asking for bean sprouts, meat balls or anything considered Southern transgression to Northern style of phở. Fresh basil, sawtooth corianders and a squeeze of lime are all that's allowed by the lady owner. Believe you me, that's all one needs to enjoy slurping the aromatic broth, chomping down on the firm, generous and succulent cooked and rare beef.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 26, 2019",
